[48.047046, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe `pip` launcher exists but its module is missing from the `/usr/local` Python installation. I'll inspect the interpreter paths, site-packages, and pip script\r\nto understand whether this is a packaging/configuration issue or missing files.\r\n\r\n```\r\necho '--- pip script ---'; head -20 /usr/local/bin/pip; echo '--- python paths ---'; python3 - <<'PY'\r\nimport sys, site, os\r\nprint('sys.executable:', sys.executable)\r\nprint('version:', sys.version)\r\nprint('prefix:', sys.prefix)\r\nprint('base_prefix:', sys.base_prefix)\r\nprint('path:')\r\nfor p in sys.path: print(' ', repr(p), os.path.isdir(p))\r\nprint('site-packages:', site.getsitepackages())\r\nprint('usersite:', site.getusersitepackages())\r\nPY\r\necho '--- local/lib listing ---'; find /usr/local/lib -maxdepth 4 -type d -name 'site-packages' -o -name 'pip*' 2>/dev/null | head -100; echo '--- \r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13 ---'; ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13 2>&1; ls -la /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages 2>&1 | head -100\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to "]
[48.047074, "o", "respond..."]
[48.047288, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
