[54.642683, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe site-packages directory contains only `pip`'s metadata, not the actual `pip` package, while Python's bundled `ensurepip` wheel is present. I'll check for \r\nconfiguration/environment causes and see whether the standard repair path works.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset +e\r\necho '--- python -m pip ---'; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\necho '--- ensurepip ---'; python3 -m ensurepip --version 2>&1\r\necho '--- env ---'; env | grep -E '^(PIP|PYTHON|VIRTUAL_ENV|PATH)=' | sort\r\necho '--- pip config ---'; pip config debug 2>&1 || true\r\necho '--- package dirs ---'; find /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages -maxdepth 2 -printf '%M %u:%g %p -> %l\\n' 2>&1 | head -50\r\necho '--- distro and dpkg ---'; cat /etc/os-release | head -5; dpkg -l 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'python3(-pip|-venv|$)' || true\r\necho '--- python module search ---'; python3 - <<'PY'\r\nimport importlib.util\r\nfor n in ('pip','ensurepip','setuptools','wheel'):\r\n    s=importlib.util.find_spec(n)\r\n    print(n, s)\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[54.64303, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
