[60.702515, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m4\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[60.702769, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThis is a corrupted installation: `pip`'s dist-info remains, but all of its module files were deleted. Since the matching pip wheel is bundled with `ensurepip`,\r\nI can safely reinstall it into the system interpreter. First I'll run `ensurepip` to repair the installation.\r\n\r\n```\r\npython3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1; echo '--- exit:' $?; echo '--- verify pip ---'; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1; pip --version 2>&1; pip3 \r\n--version 2>&1; echo '--- module ---'; python3 - <<'PY'\r\nimport pip, importlib.metadata\r\nprint('pip module:', pip.__file__)\r\nprint('pip version:', importlib.metadata.version('pip'))\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[61.438636, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
