[65.826903, "o", "\r\u001b[2K`ensurepip` sees the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata and incorrectly concludes pip is already installed. I'll remove that stale metadata, then rerun \r\n`ensurepip` so it extracts the bundled wheel and restores the missing package files.\r\n\r\n```\r\nrm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info\r\npython3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1\r\necho '--- ensurepip exit:' $?\r\necho '--- site packages ---'; find /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages -maxdepth 1 -mindepth 1 -printf '%f\\n' | sort\r\necho '--- verify pip ---'; python3 -m pip --version 2>&1\r\npip --version 2>&1\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[67.083331, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[67.083384, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\nLooking in links: /tmp/tmp2mn2posy\r\nProcessing /tmp/tmp2mn2posy/pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl\r\nInstalling collected packages: pip\r\nSuccessfully installed pip-24.3.1\r\nWARNING: Running pip as the 'root' user can result in broken permissions and conflicting behaviour with the system package manager, possibly rendering your \r\nsystem unusable.It is recommended to use a virtual environment instead: https://pip.pypa.io/warnings/venv. Use the --root-user-action option if you know what \r\nyou are doing and want to suppress this warning.\r\n--- ensurepip exit: 0\r\n--- site packages ---\r\nREADME.txt\r\npip\r\npip-24.3.1.dist-info\r\n--- verify pip ---\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n\r\n"]
