[80.384126, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m6\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[80.384893, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe pip module is restored. Now I'll verify end-to-end installation behavior using a locally built minimal wheel (so the test doesn't depend on network access),\r\nthen uninstall it to leave the system clean.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\nWORK=$(mktemp -d)\r\nmkdir -p \"$WORK/testpkg\" \"$WORK/testpkg-0.0.1.dist-info\"\r\ncat > \"$WORK/testpkg/__init__.py\" <<'PY'\r\nVALUE = \"pip repair verified\"\r\nPY\r\ncat > \"$WORK/testpkg-0.0.1.dist-info/METADATA\" <<'EOF'\r\nMetadata-Version: 2.1\r\nName: testpkg\r\nVersion: 0.0.1\r\nSummary: Local verification package\r\nEOF\r\ncat > \"$WORK/testpkg-0.0.1.dist-info/WHEEL\" <<'EOF'\r\nWheel-Version: 1.0\r\nGenerator: manual\r\nRoot-Is-Purelib: true\r\nTag: py3-none-any\r\nEOF\r\ncat > \"$WORK/testpkg-0.0.1.dist-info/RECORD\" <<'EOF'\r\ntestpkg/__init__.py,,\r\ntestpkg-0.0.1.dist-info/METADATA,,\r\ntestpkg-0.0.1.dist-info/WHEEL,,\r\ntestpkg-0.0.1.dist-info/RECORD,,\r\nEOF\r\npython3 - <<PY\r\nimport zipfile, pathlib\r\nwork = pathlib.Path(\"$WORK\")\r\nwheel = pathlib.Path(\"/tmp/testpkg-0.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\")\r\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(wheel, \"w\") a"]
[80.384922, "o", "s z:\r\n    for p in work.rglob(\"*\"):\r\n        if p.is_file():\r\n            z.write(p, p.relative_to(work).as_posix())\r\nprint(wheel)\r\nPY\r\necho '--- pip health ---'\r\npython3 -m pip --version\r\npython3 -m pip config debug\r\necho '--- install wheel ---'\r\npython3 -m pip install --no-index --no-deps /tmp/testpkg-0.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\r\necho '--- import installed package ---'\r\npython3 -c 'import testpkg; assert testpkg.VALUE == \"pip repair verified\"; print(testpkg.VALUE)'\r\npython3 -m pip show testpkg\r\necho '--- uninstall test package ---'\r\npython3 -m pip uninstall -y testpkg\r\npython3 - <<'PY'\r\ntry:\r\n    import testpkg\r\nexcept ModuleNotFoundError:\r\n    print('test package successfully uninstalled')\r\nelse:\r\n    raise SystemExit('test package still present')\r\nPY\r\nrm -rf \"$WORK\" /tmp/testpkg-0.0.1-py3-none-any.whl\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
